# The cut-over proof set: the smallest scenarios that must pass on a patched copy of the new
# build before a cut-over (docs/guides/tracking-tq.md, "Proof before the cut-over"). Same format
# as regress.list; every row is copied from it, flags included, so a row means the same thing
# in both. Run it like this:
#
#   EVE_CLIENT_DIR=tq-<N> tools/client-ci-regress.sh --list tools/client-ci/cutover.list --jobs 4
#   python3 -I tools/regress-compare.py var/regress-<last pinned run> var/regress-<this run>
#
# Coverage (tools/test_client_ci_parallel.py keeps every row in step with regress.list):
#   login and the base six     ballpark_smoke, fci_reads, lobby_guests, hud_health, capacitor
#   undock, warp               undock_distance, throttle_and_warp, fci_autopilot
#   dock                       fci_dock_range
#   market                     fci_market_trade (two clients)
#   fitting                    fci_fitfix
#   chat                       fci_chat_two (two clients)
#   asset safety               fci_upwell_safety
#   FW enlist                  fci_fw_enlist
#   ammo and HUD basics        fci_ammo_count, hud_health, capacitor
#   one bots row               fci_wing_follow
# The login path is the first five rows (ballpark_smoke, fci_reads, lobby_guests, undock_distance,
# throttle_and_warp): a must fix on it blocks a `provisional` status.
# Not covered yet: bookmarks (UpdateBookmark) and the Oris fee have no scenario; the opt-in new
# HUD has none either. Add their rows here when they exist.

ballpark_smoke
fci_reads
lobby_guests --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob
undock_distance --serial
throttle_and_warp --serial
hud_health
capacitor
fci_ammo_count
fci_dock_range
fci_autopilot
fci_fitfix
fci_market_trade --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob
fci_chat_two --with-second -- --character Alice --character Bob
fci_upwell_safety
fci_fw_enlist
fci_wing_follow --with-bots --serial -- --dev
